A||||22||Kelvin Vivian||Front license plate or not??||||1||
Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||03-19-2001||11:10 PM||||Here in California, I believe it's the law that automobiles should have their front license plates mounted... HOWEVER, I see many cars out on the roads without a front plate mounted, especially sporty cars like the new Corvette, Porsche Boxster, etc...<P>Do you think "GT" style front ends look better with or without the front plate mounted???<P>Kelvin Vivian<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd (front plateless)<BR>88 GT T-top, 5-spd (front plateless)||||reg||1
Z||000001||TwisT||03-19-2001||11:29 PM||||Without...<P>I think the plate only looks awkward on the front of a Fiero.  I got pulled over a couple years ago by a Hi-Po (going slighty over the speed limit- got a warning).  He was about to let me go when he asked me if I ever was planning to mount my plate on the front of my GT.<P>Yeah,  sure thing officer...<P>LOL<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||03-19-2001||11:46 PM||||I got pulled over once already for not having mine on (I think it looks like crap on any sports car).  Lucky that the law says I have to have a warning first.  The cop tried to tell me it was because in hit and run accidents the plate is the first thing to fall off.  I smiled and said "yeah and it helps for radar too" which is the only reason they have them IMHO.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||HAGS||03-20-2001||02:29 AM||||I got pulled over in Texas doing 77 in a 65...no front license plate, he just said be sure to get it on sometime and never said it was the law, I see many cars without it too....it fell off when I was washing my car, the hose hit it as I was pulling for slack.... he was lined up real funny looking on the left side of the highway, at first I thought it was some drunk that had slammed into the wall but then as I was passing I saw the markings and it started to turn towards me....didnt look like he was going to be able to get out the way he was positioned....I jumped over 3 lanes and took the first exit, he was right on me the whole time....wasnt trying to run from him, I really needed the exit and was being blocked on the right so I sped up to get around....3rd ticket this week...||||reg||1
