Z||000020||stsmithgt||03-21-2001||07:02 PM||||I bought my car without one.  Never had one to put on.(As if I would anyway. HA!)<BR> I suppose I'd have to get new plates if I get pulled over and hassled for it since I only have one plate to begin with. <BR> It wouldn't be the first time an attempt to ticket me for not having one was tried,"Oh yeah officer, I heard it rattling around this mourning and I didn't want to loose it so I put it in my trunk.  I'll put it back on, but I only have one bolt.  I was picking up new nuts and bolts today at work." he he. The officer still ticketed me for having cherry bomb mufflers on my 68 Galaxy after checking my tail lights, registration, license and headlights out.  I showed him the high beams and fog lights worked too with a little attitude.  He was being a real jerk because he didn't like how I took a corner. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  ||||reg||6
Z||000021||AusFiero||03-22-2001||06:25 AM||||Australian rules are different of course but I ran without a front number plate for 2 years because it looks better.<BR>Same officer pulled me over 3 times about it in a week after that.<BR>I have reluctantly refitted it but luckily we can get slimline front plates here so mounting it on the body direct (under the Fiero badge hanging over the front intake vent) rather than on the daggy facsia mount does look passable.<BR>Think it still looked better naked though. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||AusFiero||03-22-2001||06:28 AM||||Only problem with Aussie plates though...get a slimline front and you have to use the matching rear one...Have to bend the rear plate into a banana shape to fit the opening.||||reg||1
